// Local.xcconfig.example -- copy to Local.xcconfig and fill in your own team.
//
//   cp Local.xcconfig.example Local.xcconfig
//
// Local.xcconfig is git-ignored on purpose: an Apple Team ID identifies a
// specific developer account, and this repository is public. Keeping it out of
// project.yml also means `xcodegen generate` no longer wipes your signing
// selection every time the project is regenerated -- Xcode reads the value from
// here, not from the generated .xcodeproj.
//
// Your Team ID is the code in parentheses in:
//   security find-identity -v -p codesigning
// e.g. "Apple Development: you@example.com (ABCDE12345)" -> ABCDE12345
//
// Leaving it empty is fine for a simulator build; a build to a real device
// needs it (or pick the team by hand in Signing & Capabilities).

DEVELOPMENT_TEAM =
